From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Araceae Runtime <runtime@araceae.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:54:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Speak the Chat Completions wire protocol

Providers can set wire_api = "chat". Turns are still built as Responses
requests and converted for each request:

- developer and system messages before the first model output form one
  leading message; later instructions follow
  chat.mid_conversation_instructions
- namespaced and freeform tools become functions under deterministic
  aliases of at most 64 characters, which are mapped back for dispatch
- tool results directly follow their calls, and unanswered calls receive a
  placeholder result
- reasoning is replayed under chat.reasoning_field for the configured scope
- structured output, images, output token limits, and extra body fields
  follow [model_providers.<id>.chat]

Streams emit one open text or reasoning item at a time and the accumulated
tool calls when the stream ends. Context overflow, quota, and throttling are
recognized from status codes and wording, and HTTP 2xx error envelopes get
the same handling as Responses requests. Chat providers expose no hosted
tools, Responses lite, tool search, or remote compaction, and responses
without usage fall back to an estimate so auto-compaction keeps working.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
